Thu Sep 29 12:43:42 1994  Mike Warren  (msw@sampson)

	* libsw/malloc.c (extend_mem): Add sizeof(aheader_t) to _chunk_tbl
	increment.  I think this is what is causing the too-long chunk
	Warnings.  Also change ALIGN to 8, since I'm worried about the 
	comment that sizeof(header_t) must be a multiple of ALIGN.
	
	* libsw/poll.c (PollSetup): Use a static inbuf to avoid malloc.

	* libsw/batch.c (SetupBatch): Allocate all memory beforehand.
	As it was, the instk in pqsort was growing, but batch would keep
	allocating a new buffer at the end casuing the heap to be full
	of holes due to the instk reallocs.

Wed Sep 28 12:27:52 1994  Mike Warren  (msw@sampson)

	* libtree/pqsort.c (pqsort): Using a different buffering scheme
	in the loop reduces maximum memory usage by a factor of three.

	* relerr/main_nv.c (main): Add some memory reporting stuff.

	* libsw/malloc.c (malloc_used): now returns the amount of heap 
	which is in allocated blocks.  A new function named malloc_heapsz()
	returns the amount of heap malloc has obtained from the OS (which
	is what malloc_used used to do).

	* relerr/main_nv.c (main): If ctl file does not have a \cr on the
	last line, SDF_Hdrgetc will fail because some nodes (but not all)
	will call read which would return EOF, but doesn't becuase the
	file is synchronous.  I haven't fixed this.

