Thu Sep  8 09:44:11 1994  Mike Warren  (msw@sampson)

	* relerr/main_nv.c (main): Don't read or save nterms.  With
	the frac mac, the first step would be imbalanced anyway.
	(main): Clear acc, phi and nterms here, rather than in InheritSink.
	This is necessary to accumulate values during multiple calls to
	walk for the periodic bc code.

	* libtree/walk.c (WalkInit,WalkNT,WalkTerminate) Same as Walk, but 
	doesn't terminate the polling machinery until WalkTerminate.  By
	eliminating the synchronization one can do a series of imbalanced
	traversals (for instance to do periodic boundary conditions)
	without the load imbalance penalty.

	* relerr/grav_nv.c (SetGravOffset): Shift the sinks by the
	amount specified.
	
	* relerr/main_nv.c (Periodic): Enable use of periodic BC.

	* libsw/randoms.c (cube_rand): For generating cubes to test the
	periodic boundary code.

Wed Sep  7 13:14:45 1994  Mike Warren  (msw@sampson)

	* libSDF/SDF.h: Make the SDF.h in include/ a symbolic link to this.

	* libSDF/SDF-parse.y (finish_parse): Unfortunately, we need to
	be able to set the SDF datafp in either a synchronous or 
	async mode, depending on whether we are reading a huge file all
	at once, or reading small pieces independently. A new function 
	called SDF_setiomode() now exists.  The default behavior is
	unchanged.

	* libmpmy/mpmy_unixio.c (MPMY_Ftell,MPMY_Flen): Should only do 
	synchronous mode Bcast if iomode is MPMY_SINGL.

	* libmpmy/mpmy_{unixio,paragonio,cm5io}.c (MPMY_Fopen): Make 
	return value 0 if open returns -1.  We were confusing all of the
	code that assumes fopen returns NULL on failure.

	* libSDF/SDFfuncs.c: Add an MPMY_IOZERO flag to the open in SDFissdf.

Fri Sep  2 09:35:33 1994  Mike Warren  (msw@sampson)

	* libsw/Malloc.c: Warn if large malloc is attempted.  This might
	help explain abnormal behavior on a virtual memory machine like
	the paragon.

	* relerr/main_nv.c (HeapCnt) SunOS evidently has a symbol in
	the name space called HeapCnt, so we name it HeapCnt_.

	* libmpmy/mpmy_generic.c: decrease MAXCOMM to 250, and sleep
	for a second if it looks like space is short.

	* libmpmy/mpmy_nx.c: Use _isend and _irecv[x] instead of 
	plain versions.

	* libsw/malloc.c (malloc_used): New function which tells how
	much heap space has been obtained from the OS.

	* libsw/do_sigs.c: Add a PrintMemfile() to sw_handler().

